{"availability":"available","full":"geolens-io/geolens-examples","name":"geolens-examples","description":"Runnable GeoLens integrations for MapLibre, QGIS, ArcGIS, Python, TypeScript, DuckDB, STAC, OGC APIs, CLI and MCP. Every live example runs against the public demo.","category":"Developer tools","language":"HTML","stars":1,"forks":1,"created":"2026-08-13T15:58:26Z","updated":"2026-10-10T15:15:00Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://geolens-io.github.io/geolens-examples/","topics":["arcgis","examples","geojson","geolens","geopandas","geospatial","gis","leaflet","maplibre","mcp","ogc-api","ogc-api-features","openlayers","python","qgis","raster-tiles","sdk","stac","typescript","vector-tiles"],"demo":"https://demo.getgeolens.com/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T17:26:24.613Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T17:26:24.613Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T17:26:24.613Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T06:44:17.667Z","stars":1,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-08T07:32:20.050Z","stars":1,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-10T17:26:24.613Z","stars":1,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["GeoLens is a self-hosted spatial data hub: catalog, search, maps, analysis, and open APIs over data that stays on your own infrastructure. This repo holds copy-paste integrations for the tools your stack already uses. Every browser, Python, and DuckDB example reads the public demo anonymously, so you clone, open, and see it run; one constant at the top points it at your own instance. The exception is cli/, which publishes to a catalog and so runs against your own instance with a credential.","Search the catalog by meaning, connect from desktop GIS, or embed a map, with the same self-hosted catalog and open APIs underneath.","If GeoLens is useful to you, star it on GitHub. That is how most people find it. If these examples save you an afternoon, star or watch this repo too."],"features":["Live gallery: every live